Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:24:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] estuary: the system page names its columns, and long values
 of Kodi's labels take the width of the column

Seen in the real Kodi (screenshots in QEMU): the middle column of the system
page was headed "GPU" over the CPU, GPU and memory rows and the third "PVR"
over the buffers of the player; they are "Resources" and "Cache and queues"
under "System" and "Player". The screen resolution and the live bit rate
that Kodi gives are longer than a row and came out cut ("1920x1080 @ 75.00
Hz - ..."); they are rows with the value under the name.
---
